      "problem": "For the differential equation $2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy={x}^{2}-x,$ what is the associated homogeneous equation?",
      "worked_solution": "Suppose we have a second-order inhomogeneous ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe associated homogeneous equation is constructed by replacing $f(x)$ with zero:\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, in our case, the associated homogeneous equation is\n\n$$\n2{y}^{″}+5x{y}^{′}+xy=0.\n$$",
